# What Vercel does NOT need.
#
# Vercel builds the front end and nothing else: the API, the aligner and the
# acoustic models stay on the box. aligner/ alone is 2.7 GB once its venv and
# torch cache exist, so this is the difference between a 1 MB upload and a
# failed one. .gitignore already covers most of it; this file states it
# outright so the deploy does not depend on that staying true.

aligner/
server/
ops/
deploy/
supabase/
data/
scripts/warm-models.py
Dockerfile
compose.yaml
.dockerignore
.env
